      "right": "the self-firing spark — about every 0.8 s at rest"
    },
    {
      "left": "atrioventricular node",
      "right": "relays the beat after a built-in delay, so upper chambers finish emptying first"
    }
  ],
  "why": "The beat runs on its own electrical system — 'lub-dub' is just the valves slamming: first the atrioventricular pair (systole), then the outlet valves."
};

const hbOutputEstimate = {
